From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chase Haley <chasehaley33@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:08:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] PageList: reuse pages that leave the list, leave room to
 grow columns

Line pruning and column growth without reflow each destroy about one
page for every page they create. Destroying a pool page decommits it
(a memset and DiscardVirtualMemory on Windows) and the next page
faults the memory back in. Keep one zeroed page as a spare for the
next createPage instead.

Pages copied to grow the columns also get a quarter more column
capacity, so a window widened a column at a time copies its history
once per quarter instead of once per column.

On an i9-14900K at 120x32 with a 10,000-line limit, ManyLine output
recorded from ConPTY parses at 490 MB/s instead of 104 MB/s, and
resizing from 120 to 480 columns and back with full history takes
0.09 ms per step instead of 3.3 ms (worst 3.8 ms instead of 12 ms).
---
 src/terminal/PageList.zig | 185 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 179 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

